a-l-e-x-a-n-d-e-r-c-u-e-v-a-s  i'm the public information officer with  the north las vegas police department  so before we begin today's uh press  briefing i will introduce you to our  speakers  and as for that in order of appearance  it is going to be  north las vegas mayor john lee that is  spelled  j-o-h-n-l-e-e he's the mayor of the city  of north las vegas next will be council  woman pamela goins-brown  that is spelled p-a-m-e-l-a-g-o-y-n-e-s  hyphen  b-r-o-w-n  and then it will be acting police chief  jacqueline gravatt that is spelled  j-a-c-q-u-e-l-i-n-e  g-r-a-v-a-t-t  [Music]  and with that  here is merely  thank you we had an unprecedented loss  of life that happened yesterday in our  community  it was a tragedy  it was beyond sad  each of these people was a relative  a husband a wife a child a neighbor a  member of our community a very valuable  member of our community  we need to realize today that there's a  lot of grieving taking place in north  las vegas our hearts are full for these  families  we really  care when something happens in a  community that just pulls the heart  right out of it  we hope and pray that this family will  understand that this grieving process  will take them and us in the city of  north las vegas a long time  and we appreciate them understanding  that the city of north las vegas values  them and their families  thank you very much  good evening  on behalf of the city council  and our community  i wanted to extend my deepest control  condole condolences to the families of  all the victims  all of the north las vegas we mourn with  this family  we mourn with you today  this is an unfathomable tragedy  that has forever altered the lives of so  many people  our hearts and prayers are with those  who are experiencing this unimaginable  pain  their loss is our entire community's  loss  i also want to recognize our tremendous  north las vegas first responders  the care and respect that they showed  everyone involved their dedication and  compassion  the work they do is not easy  and scenes like yesterday will forever  be in their hearts  and their minds  we will hold everyone impacted by this  tragedy  in our hearts  good afternoon everyone  i wanted to update you on the facts that  we know him at this time in reference to  the multiple vehicle traffic accident  yesterday  yesterday at 3 15 we were contacted  about a multi-vehicle traffic accident  in the area of cheyenne and commerce  there were six vehicles involved and 15  individuals  there were imma go through the vehicles  in their descriptions there was a dodge  challenger who had two occupants both  who succumbed to their injuries  there was a toyota sienna van that had  seven occupants  all succumbed to their injuries  we had a ford fusion  with one adult occupant  who is currently in serious condition at  umc medical center  a chevy malibu  with one occupant  that was injured and released  a mercedes suv with two adult occupants  injured and released  and there was a ford fusion  i think i went over the fusion with the  serious  condition at umc  in this accident we do know that the  dodge challenger was traveling  northbound on commerce at a high rate of  speed it was the only vehicle traveling  northbound at this time  witnesses on scene said that the  challenger did  not stop at the red light  it went through the intersection  first striking two vehicles that were  traveling eastbound and due to that  collision three additional vehicles were  struck that were going westbound  speed was a factor  in this accident  and that is the only contributing factor  that we know of at this time  the sole vehicle heading northbound on  cheyenne  again was occupied by two individuals  due to the magnitude of this injury the  ntsb will be assisting us with this  investigation we are currently  anticipating them meeting with our  traffic division tomorrow  the heartfelt condolences to the  families and everyone affected by this  horrific incident it affects us as a  community as a valley and as a nation as  a whole  the red cross has been in contact with  our agency because they want to reach  out to those families and we are  currently diligently working on  providing those families information to  the red cross  again the north las vegas police  department the city of north las vegas  and the las vegas valley are all at a  loss  we are sending our condolences and any  support for these families that can be  expressed we encourage you to do so  thank you  last these are all very preliminary  we are anticipating getting results from  downloads of vehicles speed work up  and things of that nature the reports  from the coroner's office once we get  that information we'll be able to update  you again and provide you more specifics  but again this is extremely preliminary  we just wanted to make sure we had all  the facts as we know them right now out  to you as soon as we could thank you  i think the hardest part of this and it  may have been  just the unintentional  um  not addressing because it's extremely  tragic  the toyota sienna van had seven  occupants four juveniles and three  adults and all three all seven succumbed  to their injuries  in the accident making a total of nine  nine people that perish during this  incident  thank you  all right  i'd like to thank everyone for joining  us here as for all uh  press media outlets  you will be receiving a press release  print  for later that will have access to  photos of vehicles on scene  at this time as chief has stated this  information is very preliminary it only  happened about 24 hours ago  things have the possibility of changing  and with that there are going to be no  questions answered today okay thank you  so much and have a good day

